msgid "Playing &ksirk;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Preliminary note : the map can be scrolled by three methods. First, you can "
"put your mouse near a border of the window and the map will scroll in that "
"direction. Second, you can use your mouse wheel: With no modifier, it will "
"scroll verticaly; when pressing the Meta key, it will scroll horizontaly. "
"And lastly, you can use the keyboard arrows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Distribution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the beginning of the game, countries are distributed to all the players. "
"Each country contain one army (represented by an infantryman) at this "
"moment. Each player has some armies to distribute to his countries at her "
"turn (indicated by the presence of her name and her flag in the status bar). "
"Note that five armies are represented by a cavalryman and 10 by a cannon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To put an army on one of your countries, click on it with the left mouse "
"button. To remove an army, click with the right button. Note, as a general "
"rule, that you will never be able to remove more armies than the number you "
"already put."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a player has distributed all her armies, the next player is "
"automatically selected to do the same task. When all players have finished "
"to distribute their armies, there is two possibilities that can be selected "
"by two buttons :"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "Redistribution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ": Redistribution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One player wants to change some of his choices. The first player can then "
"remove an army he just put in a country with the right mouse button and put "
"it in another one with the left mouse button. When he finish, he gives "
"control to next player with the 'Next Player' button. When all players have "
"finished their redistribution, the two buttons are redisplayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "End of redistribution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ": End of redistribution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid "The redistribution is finished and the game can continue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fight"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After the redistribution, a game turn can start. Each player plays at his "
"turn. He has the choice to:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Next player"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid ": Give hand to the next player"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The turn of the current player finishes and it's the turn of the next one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Attack 1"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&nbsp;<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"attackTwo.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>Attack 2</phrase> </"
"textobject> </inlinemediaobject> &nbsp;<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"attackThree.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>Attack 3</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> : "
"Attack with one, two or three armies"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For a country X to attack a country Y with x armies, 2 conditions must be "
"fullfilled: 1. the two countries must be neighbours; 2. country X must have "
"at least x+1 armies before the attack. When an attack is decided, the "
"attacker must disignate the belligerants: he click on his country, drag the "
"pointer to the attacked country and \"drop it\" (release the mous button) "
"there. If the attack is valid, 2 defend buttons replace the three attack "
"ones (only one if the attacker attacks with only one army and also if the "
"defender has only one army in his country). They give the choice to the "
"defender to defend with one or two armies."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The defender choice done, the fight will happen and be solved. This will "
"described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move armies"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ": Move Armies from one country to another"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the last action of a player's turn. It gives the possibility to move "
"some armies from one of his country to another, neighbour of the first one. "
"To choose the two countries, please drag'n drop as for an attack. When both "
"countries are choosed, the \"Move armies\" group of buttons appear (see "
"below for a description of their use). Note that, before the user choose to "
"terminate the move, he can always choose to cancel it by hitting the Cancel "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "Solution of the fight"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To each army in the fight correspond a dice cast, a random number between 1 "
"and 6. The higher result of the attacker is opposed to the other one of the "
"defender. If the attacker's result is strictly higher than the defender one, "
"he wins the fight and the defender army is destroyed. Elsewhere, he looses "
"and its army is destroyed. The same happen for second higher dice of the "
"attacker if there is two or three attackers and two defenders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the number of armies in the defender country reaches 0, the ownership of "
"this country changes to the attacker: his flag is set up and one of his "
"attacking armies is installed in his new country. The \"Move armies\" "
"buttons are displayed in the toolbar to allow the attacker to move some "
"other armies from the attacking country to the newly gained one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "End of the turn"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When everybody have played, the turn is finished. Some armies are "
"distributed to the players, in function of the coutries they own: 1 for each "
"group of three countries, with a minimum of 3. There is also a bonus for "
"players that own a complete continent, different for each one. This bonus is "
"of:"
msgstr ""

